# 9. AI MONEY COACH — GEMINI INTEGRATION

Integrate Gemini using the supported Google AI SDK and a secure server-side or platform-supported secret configuration.

Never expose a private Gemini API key in frontend code or commit it to source control.

Create a dedicated conversational AI Money Coach page with:
- A polished chat interface.
- Suggested starter questions.
- Conversation history where supported.
- Streaming responses if supported by the chosen SDK.
- Clear loading and error states.
- A context panel summarizing relevant financial metrics.
- Links to relevant app sections where practical.

Suggested prompts:
- “Where did most of my money go this month?”
- “How can I reduce my spending next month?”
- “Compare my spending with last month.”
- “Am I on track to reach my savings goal?”
- “Help me create a realistic budget.”
- “What recurring expenses should I review?”

## AI behavior

Provide the coach with a structured, privacy-conscious summary of relevant transaction and budget data, rather than blindly sending all stored personal information.

The model must:
- Analyze only the data provided to it.
- Distinguish observed facts from estimates and suggestions.
- Include relevant figures and periods in its explanations.
- Never invent transactions or claim to have changed records without actually doing so.
- Never make unsupported financial predictions.
- Explain uncertainty when data is incomplete.
- Offer practical, nonjudgmental suggestions.
- Avoid presenting itself as a licensed financial adviser.
- Never request bank passwords, card PINs, or authentication secrets.

When a response references a metric, calculate that metric deterministically from application data wherever possible and pass the result to Gemini for explanation.

For transaction creation, deletion, or budget changes, use explicit user confirmation and actual application functions. Do not let a chat response pretend that an action succeeded.

If Gemini is unavailable or not configured, show a useful setup message and keep the rest of the expense tracker fully functional. Provide rule-based insights as a fallback.

